title: Gallax takes power.
subtitle: The beginning of the end?
view-if: (chancellor == royalist_chancellor or president == "Gallax" or chancellor_party == "Royalist") and rubicon_mini
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true

[? if gallax_deported and president != "Gallax" and chancellor != "Gallax": The first act that Chancellor [+ chancellor +] takes upon assuming office is bringing Adolf Gallax back to the Commonwealth, and giving him citizenship and an official cabinet position. ?]

With [+ chancellor +]'s appointment, it may seem all but over for the Unity Republic. However, people like Staal and Askew have surprisingly found themselves in the same cabinet as the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, perhaps taming is possible? Maybe we shouldn't act too rash, and bide our time.

What are we to do now?

- @fight: We will fight on the streets to prevent Gallax from taking power.
- @bide_time: We will vote against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the Assembly.

@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @bide_time: We are not ready for war. Instead, we will vote against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the Assembly.

@bide_time
subtitle: The game is not over.

The coalition is a ticking bomb, [+ royalist_chancellor +] will attempt to exercise complete power, only to be checked by Staal, who has the full confidence of President DuFour.